@@ -3,6 +3,13 @@
 Every correction is REINFORCE with a detached weight w(r) on the ratio
 r = p/q of trainer (p) to sampler (q) probabilities, per token or per
 sequence.
+
+The score is centered under the sampler (see REPORT.md): each token's update
+w(y) grad log p(y) has its expectation under the sampler's distribution q
+(top-k logprobs returned with the rollout) subtracted, so a constant offset in
+the advantage produces no expected update even when q != p. This is on by
+default; up to the top-k tail it is a no-op on-policy (q = p, w = 1) and for
+untruncated naive IS.
 """
 import math
 from typing import NamedTuple
